properties.statement:
Before the site talks about hubs, it shows one design on its own. It uses a made-up example, as the site's hand-written pages do. The example is followed from the first thing it must do, through the questions reflow2 asks, the decisions and their reasons, and the work built from them. Then it comes back again:
- code drifting from the design is caught;
- a change shows what it touches before anyone edits;
- results flow back into the design.

Each step says who does it: the person, the AI or the graph.

The home page puts the single design first and the hub as the next step. The two are named so a reader can tell them apart: "project brain" no longer names both.
